  (text "each high-pass section: 121 Hz, Q = 0.709" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 50.8 151 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "54fc5aff-d858-5334-b22a-68349e0ef2a2"))
  (text "Not part of the published circuit: the design notes' split. The DSP uses two Butterworth sections per side (fi.lowpass(2) twice,\nfi.highpass(2) twice),\na 4th-order Linkwitz-Riley pair, so the bands are in phase at Crossover and sum to an all-pass. There is no circuit behind it:\nthis is a standard analogue stand-in, all chosen. Each section is a unity-gain Sallen-Key with Q = 0.707 and a fixed 120 Hz corner\n(the DSP's default); the Crossover control would move all four corners together, which is not drawn." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 198.12 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ced0d650-ea16-5b24-a605-25d834b913e3"))
